    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The volcano covers about 51% of Hawaiʻi Island and its mass is nearly twice the combined area of all other Hawaiian islands.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        23,
        26
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.nps.gov/havo/learn/nature/mauna-loa.htm"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Mauna Loa’s eruptions often start in the summit caldera before moving into one of its two rift zones, which have historically sent lava toward Hilo and South Kona.",
